Feed a run-help file to the pager on stdin.

The help files live inside the binary, served by the in-process VFS, which
the pager (an external program) cannot see: `more $HELPDIR/print` fails
with "No such file". zsh itself can open them, so redirect and let the
pager read stdin, which every pager supports.

--- a/Functions/Misc/run-help
+++ b/Functions/Misc/run-help
@@ -29,7 +29,7 @@
     return 0
 elif [[ -n "${HELPDIR:-}" && -r $HELPDIR/$1 && $1 != compctl ]]
 then
-    ${=PAGER:-more} $HELPDIR/$1
+    ${=PAGER:-more} < $HELPDIR/$1
     return $?
 fi
 
